{"study_accession":"PRJNA868719","secondary_study_accession":"SRP391070","title":"Expression Analysis (RNA-Seq) of adult Myelodysplastic Syndromes (MDS)/Acute Myeloid Leukemia (AML) with isolated monosomy 7 compared to controls","description":"Monosomy 7 is one of the most frequent aneuploidies in myeloid malignancies, associated to heterogeneous phenotypes. Its poor prognosis differentiates it from aberrations leading to partial/complete loss of 7q region. Underlying pathogenic mechanisms are still undetermined. We performed a comprehensive epi-genomic study of karyotypically isolated monosomy 7 in adult Myelodysplastic Syndromes/Acute Myeloid Leukemias. Overall design: mRNA profiles of 18 monosomy 7 cases (Mon7), 28 controls (13 bone marrow samples from non-neoplastic cytopenias, normal bone marrow morphology and normal karyotype -CTL; 5 dic(1;7)(q10;p10) cases -DIC; 10 MDS and AML with normal karyotype - nkMN), and of CD34+ separated cells from one monosomy 7 case and one AML with normal karyotype. *************************************************************** The table below lists GEO accessions reused/reanalyzed for this study. ***************************************************************","pubmed":"","geo_series":"","n_samples":5,"samples":[{"sample_accession":"SAMN52038183","study_accession":"PRJNA868719","blood_class":"bone_marrow","class_from":"sample","title":"nkMN_4_RNAseq","description":"nkMN_4_RNAseq","sex":"","geo_sample":"GSM9267812","access":"open","dbgap":"","n_runs":1,"first_public":"2026-04-19","attributes":[["source_name","Unsorted Bone Marrow cells"],["tissue","Unsorted Bone Marrow cells"],["cytogenetics","46,XX[20]"],["age","73"],["mutations","missing"],["disease","MDS"],["geo_loc_name","missing"],["collection_date","missing"]],"runs":[{"run_accession":"SRR35659278","experiment_accession":"SRX30711304","library_layout":"PAIRED","library_selection":"cDNA","instrument_model":"Illumina NovaSeq X Plus","read_count":29083545,"base_count":87250635